  "result": {
    "text": "```python\ndef count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function count_nums which takes an array of integers and returns\n    the number of elements with a sum of digits > 0.\n    If  a number is negative, then its first digit will be  negative.\n    >>> count([-111, 11, -11]) == 1\n    >>> count_nums_nums([1, 1, 2]) == 3\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for num in arr:\n        if sum(abs(digit) for digit in str(num)) > 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```\n\nThis function iterates through each number in the array, calculates the sum of its absolute digits, and checks if the sum is greater than 0. If it is, it increments the count. The function then returns the count.",
